# Commit and push by default

After making code changes the user requested, always commit and push to the remote without waiting to be asked.

- Follow the repository's commit message style (concise, why-focused).
- Do not commit secrets (.env, credentials, etc.).
- Push to the current branch with `git push` (or `git push -u origin HEAD` if no upstream).
- Only skip commit/push when the user explicitly says not to, or when there are no changes to commit.
